# /etc/paperbot/live-telegram.env  (root:paperbot 640; made by an owner, never by install.sh). Optional.
# The real-money side writes to the owners' PRIVATE chats with the bot instead of the rule bot's room: the live paper
# bot (paperbot-combo), both executors (paperbot-executor, paperbot-executor-mexc) and the live checks
# (paperbot-livecheck, paperbot-livewatch) load this file AFTER live.env / executor.env, so the bot token stays and only
# the lines set here change. The rule bot and everything else keep live.env's room.
# Steps (docs/live1019-start-ko.md section 12, "실거래 텔레그램을 개인 채팅으로"):
#   1. each owner opens the bot in Telegram, presses Start and sends it "hi";
#   2. sudo -u paperbot bash -c 'set -a; . /etc/paperbot/live.env; cd /opt/crypto-bot-research && /opt/paperbot/venv/bin/python -m paperbot.livecheck chat-ids'
#   3. remove the "#" of the five lines below and put the ids (comma-separated) on the three chat lines.
# DANGER: a chat line left EMPTY (TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=) overrides live.env with nothing and the live bots fall back
# to the screen only. Keep a line commented out (#) rather than empty.
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=111,222
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_WARN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_INFO=
#TELEGRAM_SOUND=critical
#PAPERBOT_COMBO_TRADE_MSGS=0
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_WARN / TELEGRAM_CHAT_INFO: the same ids as CRITICAL (111,222). TELEGRAM_SOUND=critical rings only the
# alarms (🚨); "1" rings warnings too; unset or 0 keeps everything silent. PAPERBOT_COMBO_TRADE_MSGS=0: the live paper
# bot leaves its raw entry and exit lines out; the live watcher's 🟢 / 🔒 / ✅ / ❌ messages tell the trades instead.
